Best attempt score 325/70 insns (95.3%). Byte-identical twin of sub_0807B12C.

Working C that satisfies the linker and matches 67/70 instructions:
  struct S_02025FF0 { u8 _0x000[0x18C2]; u16 w; };
  extern struct S_02025FF0 D_02025FF0;   ... *(u16*)temp = D_02025FF0.w;
  final call arg: (u32)p[arg0->field_0x22*2] * 4 + arg0->field_0x14  (multiply-first!)
  p = (u8*)arg0 + 0x18; sub_080C31E4(p, (u8*)arg0+0x22, *(u32*)0x08671BB0);

Remaining 13 diffs are ALL regalloc: target keeps arg0 in r5, uses r2 for the sub_0800355C result and the 0x22 constant, r4 for p, and loads the 0x08671BB0 literal right after the strb store. Tried: declaration order (p,temp vs temp,p), `if((temp=...)==NULL)` inline, a u32 v local for the table value (385 — caused a dead second load), u32*src local (330), s16 idx local (2555, bad). Nothing moved off 325. The literal-load scheduling is the crux. Next agent: try forcing the 0x08671BB0 load to happen right after the strb store, e.g. by using the table value in a statement placed there, or restructure so agbcc keeps r0 free for it.

