Struct S_0807B12C: 0x14=u32 field_0x14, 0x18=u8[10], 0x22=s16 field_0x22, 0x24=u32, 0x38=u32, 0x3C=u32.
Remaining: regalloc — target keeps arg0 in r4 and field_0x38 in r5; computes (u8*)arg0+0x18+idx*2 as a separate pointer (adds r0,r4,#0; adds r0,#0x18; adds r0,r0,r1) then ldrb, whereas agbcc folds the 0x18 into the ldrb offset. Tried a u8* p local (427, worse) and an s16 idx local (1210, worse). Don't introduce extra locals.

Best 965/37 insns. Working C:
  struct S_0809B638 { u8 _[0x24]; u32 field_0x24; u8 _[0x10]; u32 field_0x38; u32 field_0x3C; u8 _[0xC]; u32 field_0x4C; u8 _[0xC]; u32 field_0x5C; u8 _[0xC]; u16 field_0x6C; u8 _[6]; s8 field_0x74; };
