Remaining: 1 regalloc + 1 extra/missing. Target loads the 0x08671BB0 literal into r2 then does `ldr r2,[r2]` (reusing r2); mine loads into r0 then derefs into r2. Tried inline `*(u32*)0x08671BB0` as the 3rd arg (200 — literal got merged away), a u32 v local placed after the strb (205), and v declared before the strb (225, worse). The literal must land in r2; try a `u32 *table = (u32*)0x08671BB0; ... *table` or declaring the table as extern.

Best 2090/40 insns (47.7%). Working C:
  struct S_0809BE60 { u8 _[0x14]; u32 field_0x14; u8 _[0x18]; s16 field_0x22; u8 _[0x24]; u8 field_0x5C; u8 _[3]; u8 field_0x60; };
  extern vu16 D_03000830[4];
