Only remaining diff: target loads the sub_080A5418 function pointer into r2 for the str to [r0,#0x14] (ldr r2,[pc]; str r2,[r0,#0x14]); mine loads it into r1. Everything else byte-identical. Tried: 3-arg call sub_080C31E4(arg0,1,fn) -> score 220 (extra movs r1,#1); a `void *fn` local declared first -> score 435 (extra push r4, ldr into r3); a `void **pp` local -> no effect (still 10). Need a way to make agbcc allocate the function-pointer literal to r2 at that store.

Best score 295/42 insns. Working C:
void sub_080A543C(void *arg0) {
    u8 *self = arg0;
    s16 t; s32 v;
    if (sub_080C2F24(*(s16 *)(self + 0x22), 2) == 0) {
        sub_080A5714(arg0, *(s32 *)(self + 0x4C), *(s32 *)(self + 0x5C));
    }
    D_03000830[2] = 0xFD << 6;   // extern u16 D_03000830[4];
    t = *(s16 *)(self + 0x22);
    v = (t > 0x3C) ? ((s32)(t - 0x3C) >> 1) : 0;
