Target: push {r4,lr}, r4=arg0, base 0x03000830 in r0, t in r1, and an `adds r0,r1,#0` copy before `subs r0,#0x3c`. Mine: push {r4,r5,lr}, r4=arg0 plus r5=self, base in r1, t in r0. Removing the `self` local fixes the push (push {r4,lr}) but changes regalloc elsewhere and score jumps to 480 (missing `adds r0,r1,#0`, extra `b`, `lsrs r0,r6,#0x20; lsls r0,r0,#0xc` artifacts). A local `u16 *p = D_03000830` gave 530. Need a way to keep only r4 while also getting base into r0 and an explicit temp copy before the subtract.

Best score 210/13 insns (autopilot m2c draft). Clean equivalent:
void sub_080AE09C(void *arg0) {
    void *p = *(void **)((u8 *)arg0 + 0x38);
    *(u16 *)((u8 *)p + 8) = (u16)(*(u16 *)((u8 *)p + 8) + 0x800);
