Target: ldr r2,[r0,#0x38]; ldr r0,[r0,#0x3c]; movs r3,#0x80; lsls r3,#4; adds r1,r3,#0 (copy 0x800 into r1); ldrh r3,[r2,#8]; adds r1,r1,r3; strh r1,[r2,#8]; movs r1,#0; bl sub_0801165C.
All my variants (int n=0x800, u32 val+=, volatile u16*) gave 310: agbcc hoists `ldrh r1,[r2,#8]` before the constant computation and omits the `adds r1,r3,#0` copy, leaving one instruction short. Need a way to keep the field load AFTER the 0x800 is moved into r1.

Best score 20/30 insns. Working C:
struct S_02025FF0_1870 { u8 _0[0x1870]; u32 p; };
