Only remaining diff: target pushes/pops {r4,r5,lr} but mine only {r4,lr}; all 28 body instructions are byte-identical. Everything else (including the two-literal D_02025FF0+0x1870 access, loop shape, constants 0x1B9/1, node offsets 0x30/0x3C/0x2C) matches. Need a way to make agbcc reserve r5 as a callee-saved register without adding any instructions. Tried: s32 id + u32 mask locals (pushed r5 but added an `adds r0,r5,#0` before orrs, score 691); a function-scope `u16 *tmp` local (no effect); struct-field node type (no effect).

Best score 390/44 insns (43 generated). Working C:
void sub_080B2BEC(void *arg0) {
    u8 *self = arg0;
    s32 p38 = *(s32 *)(self + 0x38);
    u8 *p3C = *(u8 **)(self + 0x3C);
    u8 *p34 = p3C + 0x34;
    u8 ***pp; u8 **p2; s32 idx; u8 *data; u16 *q; u16 v; s32 n; u8 *p28;
    sub_080113A8((void *)p38, p34);
    pp = (u8 ***)(p34 + 8); p2 = *pp;
    idx = *(s16 *)(p34 + 0xE) + *(u8 *)(p34 + 1);
    data = *p2;
    q = (u16 *)(idx * 4 + (u32)data - 4); v = q[1];
    if (v != *(u16 *)(self + 0x5C)) {
        *(u16 *)(self + 0x5C) = v;
        p28 = *(u8 **)(p3C + 0x28); *(u16 *)(p28 + 6) += 4;
        p28 = *(u8 **)(p3C + 0x28); *(u16 *)(p28 + 0xA) -= 4;
    }
    n = *(s32 *)(self + 4) + 1; *(s32 *)(self + 4) = n;
